# NO GIT LFS. This file used to route assets/**/*.png, docs/refs/*.png, docs/refs/*.gif and
# docs/progress/*.png through `filter=lfs`, contradicting DECISIONS #8 and ARCHITECTURE §8,
# which both say LFS is deferred until total asset weight passes 200 MB.
#
# It was inert only by accident: `git-lfs` is not installed on this machine (`git lfs` ->
# "not a git command"), no `filter.lfs.clean` is configured, and the attribute was not marked
# `required`, so git silently skipped the missing driver and committed the bytes plainly.
# The hazard was the future: the day anyone installs git-lfs, every PNG already committed
# stays plain while every new one becomes a pointer, and the two are indistinguishable in a
# diff. Verified asset weight today: assets/overworld is 5.12 MB across 2,506 PNGs, plus a
# 316 KB sprite atlas - three orders of magnitude under the migration trigger.
#
# Re-add the filter lines in the same commit that installs git-lfs and runs
# `git lfs migrate import`, never before.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.glb binary
